late: This tells Dart, "I promise I will initialize this variable before I use it, so don't complain about it being null right now." It’s common for Database objects or TextControllers.

async / await: These are used for tasks that take time (like reading from a database). async marks the function as "non-blocking," and await tells the code to pause there until the data is read

